他们说，这就是为什么，因为我们必须把事情做好，因为我们在其他领域如此知名，我想我们面临着巨大的压力。

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.459
But they said the same thing about Nashville.
但他们对纳什维尔也说了同样的话。

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:06.819
And they also surprisingly told me that the music scene in Los Angeles is far more not adaptable.
他们还令人惊讶地告诉我，洛杉矶的音乐界更不适应。

00:06:06.819 --> 00:06:10.740
Like it's just there's just more going on musically in LA than New York, which surprised me.
就好像洛杉矶的音乐活动比纽约更多，这让我感到惊讶。

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:11.819
Would you agree with that?
你同意吗？

00:06:11.819 --> 00:06:12.819
That is true.
确实如此。

00:06:12.819 --> 00:06:13.819
I have found New York.
我找到了纽约。

00:06:13.819 --> 00:06:18.899
I think it's a matter of like the venues are just a little more like active in LA.
我认为问题在于场馆更像是在洛杉矶举办的活动。

00:06:18.899 --> 00:06:26.100
So like I started playing music at the Hotel Cafe, which is like an incredibly intimate, you know, there's two stages.
就像我开始在酒店咖啡馆演奏音乐一样，这就像一个非常亲密的地方，你知道，有两个阶段。

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.339
The people were so nice.
人们都很好。

00:06:27.339 --> 00:06:33.779
I kept getting invited to these songwriter evenings and I'd get up and do two or three songs and meet people who ended up becoming collaborators.
我不断被邀请参加这些歌曲作者之夜，我会起床创作两三首歌，并遇到最终成为合作者的人。

00:06:33.779 --> 00:06:34.620
It was great.
太棒了。

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:35.459
Yeah.
是的。

00:06:35.459 --> 00:06:36.300
That is fun.
那很有趣。

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:41.699
First of all, it's so nice to not to have to do one thing, not that you have to do acting, but you know what I mean?
首先，不用做一件事真是太好了，不是说你必须演戏，但你知道我的意思吗？

00:06:41.699 --> 00:06:43.579
It's what you were saying earlier.
这就是你之前说的。

00:06:43.579 --> 00:06:45.100
I feel very aligned with that.
我对此非常认同。

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:48.980
I like to get to do a lot of different things because otherwise I'll get to bored.
我喜欢做很多不同的事情，否则我会感到无聊。

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:57.180
And what I've noticed by doing a lot of things, I mean, it could be ADD or however you want to frame it, Or it could just be like artistic behavior, you know?
我通过做很多事情注意到，我的意思是，它可能是ADD，或者你想如何构建它，或者它可能只是像艺术行为，你知道吗？

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:00.660
Like the life of an artist is like, you kind of have to spread yourself around a little.
就像艺术家的生活一样，你必须稍微分散一下自己。

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.019
It's not always one thing.
这并不总是一回事。

00:07:02.019 --> 00:07:04.459
I guess unless you're Van Gogh, it was one thing.
我想除非你是梵高，否则这是一回事。

00:07:04.459 --> 00:07:08.180
But I'm sure he had other tricks up his sleeve too, that we probably don't know about.
但我确信他还有其他的伎俩，只是我们可能不知道。

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:11.740
But I would say that, and then the artistry kind of bleeds into each other.
但我想说的是，然后艺术性就会相互渗透。

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.379
Would you say that that's true?
你说这是真的吗？

00:07:13.379 --> 00:07:18.779
For me, it's kind of like, I think about, there's just like different ideas need a different form.
对我来说，这有点像，我想，不同的想法需要不同的形式。

00:07:18.779 --> 00:07:22.100
Like sometimes I have an idea and I'm like, well, that's a 90 minute story.
就像有时我有一个想法，然后我想，好吧，这是一个 90 分钟的故事。

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.060
Like that's a movie.
就像那是一部电影。

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.180
I have another idea, and I'm like, that's a four-minute song.
我有另一个想法，我想，那是一首四分钟的歌。

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:27.300
I'm not gonna get anything more.
我不会再得到任何东西了。

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:32.459
